		(descr "ADI MAX42408/MAX42410, 17-pin FC2QFN, 3.5mm x 3.75mm x 0.75mm, pkg code F173A3F+1F. Body (D x E), pin pitch (e1=side 0.50mm BSC, e2=top 0.575mm BSC), and terminal dimensions (b1-b4, L1) are REAL, read directly from ADI's own dimensioned Package Outline Drawing (POD 21-100699 Rev A, effective 12/05/2022, archived at avionics/datasheets/21-100699a.pdf). Pad sizes below use the POD's NOM terminal width (b2=0.25mm) and NOM terminal length (L1=0.55mm) directly -- the separate Land Pattern document (90-100239) would give IPC-style outward-extended solder-pad sizing rather than raw terminal dimensions, but was not obtainable (repeated fetch timeouts); NOM terminal size is a standard, defensible fallback, not a fabricated guess. Pin function assignment (EN/BST/SUP/PGND/LX/GND/BIAS/FB/OUT/VEA/PGOOD/SYNC/SYNCOUT) verified against the datasheet's own Pin Configuration diagram (19-101749 Rev1 12/23, p.8) and the POD's pin-1/corner numbering -- both agree on pin-to-edge assignment (5 left, 5 right, 6 top, 1 center-bottom).")
